commonMistakes:
  - title: "Relying on Simple Whitespace Splitting"
    description: "Using text.split(' ') counts standalone punctuation, double spaces, and emojis as separate words. Accurate counts require Unicode letter tokenization."
  - title: "Assuming 300 WPM Reading Speed"
    description: "While 300 wpm is commonly claimed, empirical cognitive meta-analyses (Brysbaert 2019) establish the standard adult silent reading benchmark at 225 wpm."
  - title: "Confusing Characters With and Without Spaces"
    description: "Social media, translation agencies, and character-limited forms distinguish between total glyphs with spaces and printable characters without spaces."
  - title: "Miscounting UTF-16 Emoji Surrogate Pairs"
    description: "In basic JavaScript, emoji surrogates register as 2 characters. Accurate length calculation requires Array.from(text) or regex unicode code point counting."
sources:
